A||||8||Rare87GT||Heater in a Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Rare87GT||11-09-2001||02:22 AM||||Is there anyway for the heater to work better in my car.  It is starting to get colder here in Wichita, KS and I need some warm air.  My heater takes like 10 minutes to get warm.  Can I like get a upgrade on a heater or something that pumps some hot air a little quicker so I don't get frost bite? <P>------------------<BR>1987 GT *5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||11-09-2001||02:26 AM||||You should definately do something about that, when working correctly, the Fiero heater heats up incredibly quickly.  My friends give me a lot of jokes about that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>With the Fiero fire connection and all.<BR>Good luck,<BR>Mike<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cheer_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-09-2001||02:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rare87GT:<BR><B>Is there anyway for the heater to work better in my car.  It is starting to get colder here in Wichita, KS and I need some warm air.  My heater takes like 10 minutes to get warm.  Can I like get a upgrade on a heater or something that pumps some hot air a little quicker so I don't get frost bite? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, you can replace your heater core with new one & give your cooling system a good flush. I just did that to my winter driver & it heats up much quicker & hotter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good Luck<BR>-Haze   <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Formula88||11-09-2001||01:05 PM||||Make sure you have a good thermostat and it's not leaking around the thermostat seal.  That'll cause your engine to warm up more slowly.  I'd also run the stock 195* thermo in the winter if you're concerned with heater output.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-09-2001||04:48 PM||||I just replaced the heater core on my GT.  It's plenty warm.  You need to make sure that your hot/cold selector is actually operating the valve to allow flow thru the heater core.  Mine was really stiff and although it moved it wasn't fully opening.<BR>Gary<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||CoolBlue87GT||11-09-2001||05:14 PM||||LOL, Oh my gosh! Your not going to believe this, <BR>but I thought your post said "Heather in a Fiero"<P>LOL<P>She would help keep you warm !!!!<p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 11-09-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000006||WhiteFieroBlur||11-09-2001||07:53 PM||||I got my heater core replaced but I have a problem, its blowing air back into the front conpartment. Its not suppose to do this right? There is like a hole up front around where the heater core goes that looks like it should be covered up. My car doesn't get warm at all cause of this I think. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||11-10-2001||02:16 PM||||As I remember.... there should be a foam gasket that seals the hole the heater tubes go thru. If that's missing you'll loose allot of air thru it.<P>A slow heater could be bad, need flushing, or just air locked. Try the heater bleed portion of the coolant filling procedure in my cave. (engine menu)<P>Also, don't run the blower on high. Slowing the blower gives more time to heat the air as it passes thru the luke warm heater core.<P>As indicated above, make sure it's got a good 195 thermostat as well. A 180 will reduce available heat for the core.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroMontreal||11-10-2001||02:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>LOL, Oh my gosh! Your not going to believe this, <BR>but I thought your post said "Heather in a Fiero"<P>LOL<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I though I read the same thing! LOL<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> ||||reg||1
